# Code Review

When asked to review code in this repository:

- Use `docs/CODEBASE_STANDARDS.md` as the rubric; cite the specific rule when
  flagging a violation.
- Priority order: correctness bugs > standards violations > security issues >
  missing tests > simplification opportunities.
- Every finding needs: severity (blocker / should-fix / nit), file and line,
  what is wrong, and a concrete suggested fix.
- Only report real findings — no padding, no generic praise, no speculative
  issues you cannot point to in the diff.
- End with a verdict: approve, approve-with-nits, or request-changes.
